  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sahara Expo Egypte 2024</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Sahara, the International Agricultural Exhibition for Africa and the Middle East, is the main platform for agriculture, animal production, and aquaculture in the MENA (Middle East and North Africa) region.In the combi-track, a Dutch pavilion and trade mission on climate and water smart agriculture to the Sahara Expo, was included in the activities. The &quot;Climate and Water Smart Agriculture (CaWSA)&quot; combi-track focusses on linking Egyptian, Dutch, and international companies, entrepreneurs and institutes, fostering trade, innovation, and entrepreneurship in the area of climate and water smart agriculture. This track works towards a resilient, future-proof farming system in Egypt, in which farmers, youth and women in particular, thrive.The goal of this project is to participate with a Dutch pavilion at the Sahara Expo with Dutch horticulture and agro-food companies, as well as governmental and knowledge institutes.This will create the following opportunities:&#x2022;	Business opportunities between Dutch companies and Egyptian/MENA companies;&#x2022;	Knowledge exchange between Egyptian and Dutch companies on climate and water smart agriculture via a 3-day seminar programme;&#x2022;	Enhanced possibilities for further cooperation;&#x2022;	Promotion of selected Dutch funded programmes and activities in the agriculture sector in Egypt and identifications of new partnerships and activities between the Netherlands and Egypt (and the MENA region by extension) in the field of agriculture and horticulture, under the Dutch combi-track approach;&#x2022;	Positioning of the Netherlands, and its companies, as the partner in sustainable, innovative, climate smart and circular agriculture and horticulture.</narrative>
  </description>
